  "worked_solution": "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type I region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-0\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x[y]_{y=-2}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,(2-(-2))\\,dx \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx \\\\  & =-4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{x=0}^{x=\\pi } \\\\  & =-4(-1-1) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
